This source milestone expanded Brainstash's local authoring workflow.

- **Media library** — a page for uploaded media, with working upload.
- **Dynamic content blocks** — a live dynamic-block authoring UI plus settings.
- **Server-side Markdown rendering** — HTML is sanitized before it is stored and displayed.
- **Stats & profile** endpoints.

The frontend moved to **cookie-based authentication**. Query parameters and
media upload were repaired, and the public-facing suite name changed to Aylith.

The earlier paired entry and category stills were withdrawn from this entry.
Their example data, dates and view counters have no documented release fixture;
one category still even reads “0 categories total” above four visible rows.
They cannot establish the current product state. Fresh matched light/dark
captures and narrated films of a verified local workflow remain release work.

## Current source-run study · September 25, 2026

These newer paired captures are from the **actual locally run Brainstash app**, using a disposable SQLite database and a fictional account. They show a later source state, not footage from the June milestone. A fictional reference was saved, edited, found by a title/content search for `parser`, and opened on its History page. The saved note's source uses a reserved `.example.test` address. No private note, uploaded media, hosted account or production database appears.

The [public Brainstash source overview](https://aylith-labs.github.io/brainstash/) explains this workflow and its setup boundary. It is a static page, not a hosted knowledge base or sign-in service.

